-- title:
--   At q=2 the level-4M' q-expansion field descends to level M'
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 2$, let $M'$ be a positive natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$. Write $\Gamma$ for [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ obtained by pushing forward along the inclusion of $\Gamma_0(q^2M')$ the preimage under `gamma0Units (q ^ 2 * M')` of the subgroup `levelH q M'` of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$, the latter being the kernel of the unit reduction map `ZMod.unitsMap` attached to the divisibility $q \mid q^2M'$, that is the units reducing to $1$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ (for $q = 2$ the whole unit group, so $\Gamma = \Gamma_0(4M')$). The assertion is an equality of intermediate fields of the Laurent series field $\kappa((q))$: the field `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, namely the $\kappa$-subfield generated by the set `intFormRatiosC κ Γ`, coincides with `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`, the $\kappa$-subfield generated by the two series `jqModC κ` — the reduction into $\kappa$ of the integral $q$-expansion of $j$, with its pole term $q^{-1}$ — and `jqNModC κ M'`, its image under the substitution $q \mapsto q^{M'}$.
--
--   This is the characteristic-$2$ degeneration statement for the $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_0(4M')$: modulo $2$ the Igusa level structure at $q$ contributes nothing, and the component of the reduction through the cusp $\infty$ has function field $\kappa\bigl(j(q), j(q^{M'})\bigr)$, the level-$M'$ modular function field. It feeds the genus computation [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.genusFF_xHFunctionFieldC_levelH_eq_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.genusFF_xHFunctionFieldC_levelH_eq_of_eq_two).
